<!--Post: 11314--><!--Time: 1110582384-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11314"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 3:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There are a few post-arrest threads on “Catch” speculating on when and where Rader began killing. <BR> <BR>Steve-Huff initiated this one postulating that Petra and &#40;Chris&#41;Tina may have been Greeks. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/11/693.html?1110478836" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/11/693.htm l?1110478836</a> <BR> <BR>This one started by HBcontrol is looking at what little we know of Rader’s Air Force career. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/11/696.html?1110557318" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/11/696.htm l?1110557318</a> <BR> <BR>This is where I found the inspiration to kick off a new thread. <BR>Hey, everybody’s doing it! <BR> <BR>A post by Steve_huff ties what is known of Rader’s service record to this “Message From BTK” on 12/9 by Christ on the Cross <BR> <BR>“TO address the connection between myself and op. &#34;Barn door&#34;, I would say that this is false. My duty in the military consisted of radio work which kept my in the field and allowed for several opportunities to kill others. After I was discharged, I went about returning/becoming to/a “normal” citizen. I soon found that I was not able to cope with certain events during my service, although I need to say that my inability to cope was not wholly negative. I believe I had longed for a more intimate, and therefore finalizing, encounter when killing. Here is where pictures would have helped. I needed to rationalize and fantasize about the acts I had committed; I needed to be able to remember every detail. I had to try again…the whole aura of death and my passion to posses it for everyday use became amazingly consuming. All in all I always believed I would stop, and I did…I still remember my favorite, Vicki Wegerle. I did not plan this one per se as I had the others…a &#34;lapse of control&#34; I always called that one, felt the best as well. I strangled her and left…BUT I CAME BACK! I took one more picture and then walked away…yes down Arrowhead St.” <BR> <BR> <BR>I am sold. This rambling semi-literate post is Rader’s work. <BR> <BR>My belief is that he is describing BTK’s beginnings. He also alludes to an ending -- or more specifically, an outcome. <BR> <BR>Additionally: <BR> <BR>Rader confirms his military service <BR>&#40;I’m beginning to lose track. How many suspect subsets intersect now? Coleman, WSU, WPD reject, military service, radio man… &#41; <BR> <BR>He hints that his tour of duty or his affliction is NOT related to the war in Southeast Asia <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.cpcug.org/user/billb/ranchhand/ranchhand.html" target=_top>http://www.cpcug.org/user/billb/ranchhand/ranchhan d.html</a> <BR> <BR>He discloses that he was in the rear with the gear and NOT in combat <BR> <BR>…Which leads to the most worthwhile topic of discussion regarding this post, <BR> <BR>He admits to multiple homicides while stationed overseas. <BR> <BR>“My duty in the military… allowed for several opportunities to kill others” <BR> <BR>When he is stateside again, he has this revelation: <BR> <BR>“… After I was discharged… I believe I had longed for a more intimate, and therefore finalizing, encounter when killing...” <BR> <BR>I interpret this to mean that his overseas victims spoke little or no English. <BR>This would have made it easier for Rader to objectify his early victims. <BR>We know from Kevin Bright that Rader initiated banal conversations. <BR> <BR>“Haven’t I seen you at the University?” <BR> <BR>Did this kind of discourse create the “intimacy” Rader “longed for”? <BR>Was humanizing his Wichita victims the key to “finality”? <BR>It has been suggested that he made audio-tapes in addition to taking photographs. <BR> <BR>I am convinced that, as BTK, Rader needed to give orders, build rapport, placate and lie, taunt and threaten.  <BR>Given Rader’s religious upbringing, I don’t think it too farfetched that he &#40;mis&#41; quoted scripture or prayed aloud as part of his ritual. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _  <BR> <BR>Okinawan’s have the lowest per capita income in Japan. <BR>An enlisted man stationed on Okinawa in the 60s needed only a 3 day pass and a paycheck to live like a wealthy hedonist. <BR>The vices and fulfillments of privileged men were bargain temptations for young soldiers. <BR> <BR>Shibari Kinbaku is a celebrated form of Japanese rope bondage. <BR>I am no expert on this subject. <BR>Heck, I flunked out of Weblos because of the dadblasted knots! <BR>I hesitate to post any links on Shibari due to the explicit subject matter. <BR>I did, however, find a somewhat scholarly &#40;albeit racially hamhanded&#41; blog on the history of Shibari Kinbaku. <BR>According to the author it is intended to render the captive powerless and motionless. <BR>The ties, which traditionally use hemp rope, possess an aesthetic quality. <BR>Shibari is considered an erotic and sculptural artform by some. <BR>Total stillness of the subject is a prime objective. <BR>Introspective soul searching is expected of the captive. <BR>Sado-masochistic Shibari is desended from methods of torture used in the Edo period of Japanese History. <BR> <BR>So, while I feel that Dennis Rader developed a bondage fetish from studying the lurid covers of True Detective magazine at the Rexall, <BR>I’m convinced that he experienced it in the flesh in Okinawa… for the first time. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>.”… I always believed I would stop, and I did …” <BR> <BR>Is Rader trying to imply that Vicki Wegerle was his last hit? He seems to indicate that he has arrested his urges despite suffering a “lapse of control”. <BR> <BR>Rader identifies himself as Christ on the Cross, and lists his fictitious email address as <a href="mailto:BeatTheKing@neverwill.ever">BeatTheKing@neverwill.ever</a> <BR> <BR>I always interpreted self pity and arrogant posturing in those monikers. <BR> <BR>“I am Christ-like in my suffering. BTK is the king and you’ll never catch me” <BR> <BR>Here’s another way to look at it. <BR> <BR>“I am part of the body of Christ. He died for my sins. Though I have and will continue to escape the laws of man – BTK never will ever escape the ultimate judgment of Christ the King.” <BR> <BR>Does Rader believe in God? Or… does he mock spirituality? <BR>Can a true sociopath harbor a belief in God’s love?… in God’s wrath? <BR>Even the devil himself knows he is playing a losing game.  <BR> <BR>Did Dennis Rader envision his own unavoidable outcome? <BR> <BR>Discuss. <BR> <BR>LD  <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>P.S. <BR> <BR>I found this link regarding the U.S. in Okinawa over on AMW. It is quite interesting. Whether it is based in fact, I can not say.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://hnn.us/articles/2867.html" target=_top>http://hnn.us/articles/2867.html</a> <BR> <BR>However, if anyone wants to blame the military for BTK or rant about U.S. imperialism, please start another thread… back on AMW would be a good place to do that. <BR> <BR>Thanks, <BR> <BR>RunningDog <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
