<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11319"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 3:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The information may certainly fit, but the style of writing is much different than that of Dennis as published by the media.  <BR> <BR> Could be he purposely mixed tenses, etc. and mispelled on &#34;media&#34; letters, and typed in his true style on message board posts?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11319-->
<!--Post: 11321--><!--Time: 1110585281-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11321"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 3:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nah, not sold. The writer offers no new information on additional killings in the Wichita area and is only describing killings that were previously known before the arrest of Dennis Rader. It implies that they stopped killing and came back one more time to kill and that Wegerle in 1986. Dennis Rader has been charged with two additional murders after 1986 so he clearly didn&#39;t stop and they suspect but have not charged him in an additional three murders. Anyone could have speculated reasons for killing and come up with a background and military occupation and many posters were doing just that at the time and speculating that he had a military background so although the specialty occupation in the military may have turned out to be close to accurate it is only coincidental. I&#39;m not sold on the Christ-on the Cross name either. Also there are way too few gramatical errors in that post to have been written by Dennis Rader.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
