<!--Post: 11349--><!--Time: 1110603280-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11349"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 8:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the Dog is sniffin&#39; a good trail.  That post had several screwy angles that fit very well now that we know the real BTK.  Johno makes some good points, though, so I&#39;m not betting the whole shack on it.  If it&#39;s a poser, it was a poser with some very good luck or some better-than-poser-average insight, IMO.  If the matter isn&#39;t already settled by computer forensics that will &#40;hopefully&#41; come out eventually, then I think it will become apparent when more Rader writing samples become known.  I may even start a thread to collect those.  Anyway, it would only take a few similarities to sell me.  If you could show me a known Rader writing of any kind that uses any instance of the rather anal-retentive &#34;returning/becoming to/a&#34; construction &#40;a1/b1 a2/b2&#41;, I would buy it totally.  That&#39;s rather rare. <BR> <BR>I also love the capitalized &#34;TO...&#34; at the beginning.  Apart from when I was reading fairy tales to the kids, the last time I saw that was....in a BIBLE AT CHURCH.  Looks to me like another BTK-track in the mud by the river.... <BR> <BR>I think there are more bodies, but I don&#39;t know where they&#39;re buried.  If they&#39;re in the Land of the Rising Sun, however, then it&#39;s a major embarrassment for Uncle Sam, and it&#39;s no small wonder they&#39;re locking down at 10 until damage control is in place. <BR> <BR>As to Rader&#39;s spirituality, I&#39;m at a loss.  I would discuss if I could, but it&#39;s all speculation, and the whole thing is just mind-numbing.  I know this much - although men and women may hate his sins worse than mine, it doesn&#39;t make mine any less than his, or his any worse than mine.  Just looking at what is known about his own family, he&#39;s done a better job with raising them up right than I&#39;ve done with mine.  For all the evil he has surely done, he may have also done more good than I did.  A sobering thought.  That&#39;s my confession for the night.   <BR> <BR>BACK to the subject, I don&#39;t know where that leaves the &#34;Christ on the Cross&#34; and &#34;Beat the King&#34; references, assuming it was BTK.  I&#39;ve bounced back and forth on that one, too.  I agree with the posted interpretations of those thoughts, which are almost as two-sided as...... <BR> <BR>.....a church-going serial killer. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
