<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11352"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 9:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->....but also see <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/76/698.html?1110520913" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/76/698.htm l?1110520913</a> for the beginnings of an analysis of his writings &#40;looks like it&#39;s already starting&#41;.  Unless Rader polished the heck out of that post &#40;would love to see his legal submissions&#41; then the &#34;Christ&#34; post may be out of his league, grammar-wise.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11352-->
<!--Post: 11358--><!--Time: 1110607840-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11358"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 10:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think <u>far</u> too much credence is given to the seemingly half-educated nature of Rader/BTK&#39;s first correspondence. <BR> <BR>I posted at ks.com under three different nics for the last several months, and virtually every person I told was flabbergasted - and it <b>wasn&#39;t that hard</b>. If anything, developing a kind of persona on paper or on this computer screen is far, far easier to do than trying to do it while interacting with others. I was Larry Anderson, thundersaid, and a_bracksis. In my opinion, it&#39;s not like I even tried to hide my light under a bushel all that much. I tended to let Larry be the intellectual; I pictured him as an pointy-headed but gregarious and affable nerd, a pocket-protector wearing kind of guy with an old-fashioned radio announcer&#39;s speaking voice. Then there was thundersaid, the &#34;entity.&#34; He was sometimes just cryptic, borderline poetic, but occasionally swung down out of his cloud and commented normally. a_bracksis was a smart-aleck and a bit of a troll, but not seriously so. He was the most over-sensitive of the bunch. Yet, all three tended to spell well - which I do - all three used phrases that Steve_Huff uses. All three made, on occasion, observations similar to ones Steve_Huff had. I didn&#39;t even try all that hard to hide who I was, is what I&#39;m saying. <BR> <BR>But if you&#39;re Denny Rader, and you understand that your sadistic pursuits make you an animal in the eyes of society, but you have a controlling, domineering side that demands you be an example, outwardly, of some kind of legal rectitude, you obviously know you&#39;ve got to conceal whenever possible your real identity. John Douglas, when writing about BTK in one of his profiling books, stated that he noted a marked improvement in each letter BTK sent to police. <BR> <BR>And Rader was able to easily pass every day of his life until February 25th, 2005, as a relatively &#34;normal&#34; person. Some people loved him, some thought he was an a$$. A fact that would not be significant at all if he were just some dog catcher dude. He was able to kill a little boy and little girl &#40;Oteros&#41; and then raise his own children, even seeming like a &#34;doting&#34; father in the eyes of some. <BR> <BR>So I think it&#39;s sensible to drop this concept of Rader as the semi-dyslexic verbal &#39;tard when it came to expository writing. He was average in his verbal ability, and frankly, the stilted nature of the wording in that ChristOntheCross post fits with what we are learning about the man. If anything, the letter we&#39;ve all known about for years, the one claiming credit for the Otero murders, was either intentionally dumbed down or an example of a rushed, nervous, unskilled typist, using an old typewriter, likely.  <BR> <BR>I have to agree; if the ChristOntheCross poster was a faker, he scored a scary hit on the specialty in the military. I have 10 years background in broadcasting, and have heard of general work related to communications towers and the tech supporting them referred to in a blanket way as &#34;radio work&#34; before.  <BR> <BR>I won&#39;t convert a hardcore skeptic with this, and do hold out the possibility I could be wrong...but the correlation between CotC&#39;s post and what we now know about Rader&#39;s tour of duty is a little beyond coincidence, in my opinion.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11358-->
<!--Post: 11364--><!--Time: 1110609257-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11364"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 10:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->True, that post has some serious flaws on a close examination.  Above all else is the basic accuracy in describing his life.  The key verifier for me is a pre-Otero murder.  If Rader becomes a credible suspect in at least one murder during his service years, then I would say the post was written by either Rader or Rader&#39;s guardian devil.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
