</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 11:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E. I am in agreement with you on that one. Has anyone figured out which post on this board he may have been replying to? It always struck me as being a reply to something written somewhere, and within say, the month previous to that post. <BR>I have not been able to say this before, but I was told back around Christmas that it was believed that the real BTK had posted 6 times on this board, and that 2 had been traced to colleges in the Wichita area. No one except WPD and BTK know if this post is one of them, but I feel that it can not be excluded yet. <BR>A couple of points that previous posters on this thread have made need a little rebuttal. <BR>1: His statement that he was not involved in &#34;Barn Door&#34; does not to me indicate that he was not posted in Southeast Asia. That was but one small component, the spraying of agent orange. <BR>2: I have read that post since the first day I got on this board, and I still see nothing that says that Wergle was his &#34;last&#34; victim. He said that he always thought that he could stop and he did. The proximity of that statement to the comments about Vicki should not indicate connectivity. I feel that writer has a good command of his thoughts, and was fully capable of connecting the two. I see no evidence of that. I see them both as stand-alone statements. <BR>E. Why certainly you can change your opinion. Hasen&#39;t everyone here at one time? You should see what we are discussing on the A&amp;E board right now. A very credible person &#40;active LE&#41;, is suggesting that maybe EAR-ONS were two different perps. How&#39;s that for sending your train of thought down a different track?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
